			"type": "text",
			"text": "Dickosteus was a placoderm discovered in Orkney and Caithness counties of Scotland, dating back to the Devonian. Its name is a reference to Robert Dick, a naturalist and amateur geologist and the Greek word for Bone. It was about 43.7 centimeters long. Dickosteus is important to science as its one of the few placoderms known from a full skeleton, giving us an idea about their body plan."
